        "original_id": "37037e82-7e4b-5adb-aba5-cec73b46ac31",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alan Dean Foster, Samuel R. Delany\n- Works: Star Wars: The Force Awakens (novel), the 1976 novelization of the first Star Wars film\n- Roles: writer, author, professor, literary critic\n- Topics: fantasy, science fiction, film novelizations, memoir, criticism, essays on sexuality and society\n\nFacts:\n- Samuel R. Delany was born on April 1, 1942, and is an American author, professor, and literary critic.\n- Alan Dean Foster was born on November 18, 1946, and is an American writer of fantasy and science fiction.\n- Samuel R. Delany is known to friends as Chip Delany.\n- Samuel R. Delany's work includes fiction, especially science fiction, as well as memoir, criticism, and essays on sexuality and society.\n- Alan Dean Foster has created and contributed to book series and has written more than 20 standalone novels.\n- Alan Dean Foster is especially prolific as a writer of film-script novelizations.\n- Alan Dean Foster wrote the 1976 novelization of the first Star Wars film.\n- Alan Dean Foster is also the author of Star Wars: The Force Awakens (novel).",
